<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<root>
	<Operation>standard</Operation>
	<!-- After every run, review.html (in that run's results folder) shows the changed and new cards with rule
	     checks. true = open it in the browser automatically; false = just write it. -->
	<OpenReviewPage>true</OpenReviewPage>
	<!-- VALID OPERATIONS: 
	<Operation>standard</Operation>
	<Operation>massnerfpoison</Operation>
	-->
	<!-- FOLDERS: relative paths here and below start at the "main folder", the folder this config.xml is in.
	     Data:    your update files (the default update file is data\updatefile.txt).
	     Results: one folder per run, named by date and time, with review.html and a copy of every card changed.
	     Logs:    everything the tool prints, one file per day (yyyy-MM-dd.log); runs on the same day are added to it.
	     CleanupMonths: at the start of each run, anything in these three folders that hasn't changed for this many
	     months is deleted. 0 = never delete. The update file in use is always kept, and a folder that holds the
	     game data (PathToCardXMLs, or any cards_section files) is never cleaned. -->
	<Folders>
		<Data>data</Data>
		<Results>results</Results>
		<Logs>logs</Logs>
		<CleanupMonths>3</CleanupMonths>
	</Folders>
	<PathToCardXMLs>C:\Users\purpl\OneDrive\Documents\TU_Test</PathToCardXMLs>
	<StandardOperationConfig>
		<PathToUpdateFile>data\updatefile.txt</PathToUpdateFile>
		<AutoStats>
			<!-- 
		WHAT THESE MEAN:
		
		When you provide the generator with stats, it gives it the stats for the max level of the highest tier (which you entered)
		PercentAcrossTier is "how much, as a linear percent, should the stats drop off between max level of the tier and level 1".
		PercentBetweenTiers is to give a big, splashy reason to fuse cards.  Basically, it enforces a gap between level 1 of a tier and max level of the prior tier.
		So, as an example, using the default values of 15 and 5:
		
		Tier 3 Level 6 has 100% of stats
		Tier 3 Level 1 has 85% of stats
		Tier 2 Level 6 has 80% of stats
		Tier 2 Level 1 has 65% of stats
		Tier 1 Level 6 has 60% of stats
		Tier 1 Level 1 has 45% of stats.
		-->
			<PercentAcrossTier>15</PercentAcrossTier>
			<PercentBetweenTiers>5</PercentBetweenTiers>
		</AutoStats>
		<Scaling>
			<!--
		Mode: autostats (the percentages above) or tiered (the ranges below).
		The update file can switch to tiered part way through with a comment, e.g.
		  // SCALE: 50..60, 60..80, 80..100
		and back to this setting with
		  // SCALE: DEFAULT

		TIERED: each fusion level gets a range of the max values you type.  Level 1 of that
		tier gets the first number, the tier's max level gets the second, levels between are
		spread evenly.  A card uses the range for its own fusion level (the top card's
		<fusion_level>, none = 0, counting down the chain).  A four-stage commander scales its
		last three stages and leaves the first unchanged; add a fourth range (FusionLevel0..3,
		the first being for that extra lowest stage) to scale it too.  Summoned cards (after a line of three or
		more dashes in the update file, or in set 9500) use Summoned on every tier.
		Values round to the nearest whole number, minimum 1.  A max of 0 stays 0 at every level.
		-->
			<Mode>autostats</Mode>
			<Tiered>
				<FusionLevel0>50..60</FusionLevel0>
				<FusionLevel1>60..80</FusionLevel1>
				<FusionLevel2>80..100</FusionLevel2>
				<Summoned>50..100</Summoned>
			</Tiered>
		</Scaling>
		<NewCards>
			<!--
		NEW CARDS: blocks in the update file with a Picture: line (or after "// NEW: TRUE") are built
		as complete new cards, the way CardBuilder does: every level, an id block from the section
		file's "Lowest ID available" header, fusion recipes and picture replacements.
		SetId: set for new cards, unless the card has a Set: line or a "// SET: n" comment applies.
		SectionFile: the section file that receives new cards and holds the next-id header.
		Label: written as a comment around the new cards and recipes.  Leave empty to use the
		update file's name and the month, e.g. "updatefile - October 2026".
		-->
			<SetId>2500</SetId>
			<SectionFile>cards_section_21.xml</SectionFile>
			<Label></Label>
		</NewCards>
	</StandardOperationConfig>
	<MassNerfPoisonConfig>
		<Factor>.4</Factor>
	</MassNerfPoisonConfig>
</root>